    "title": "Trump Says Path to Ukraine Peace Talks Unclear After Kremlin Meeting",
    "text": "• Donald Trump stated the path ahead for Ukraine peace talks is unclear following a meeting between Russian President Vladimir Putin and US envoys.\n• The meeting at the Kremlin involved US special envoy Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner, with a subsequent meeting planned between Kushner and Ukrainian negotiator Rustem Umerov in Florida.\n• Trump said Putin wants a deal, but the outcome is uncertain.\n• The Kremlin stated Putin accepted some US proposals but compromises haven't been found.\n• A major hurdle remains: the fate of four Ukrainian regions Russia partially occupies.\n• Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy has ruled out giving up territory.\n• Negotiations have intensified as Ukraine faces setbacks on the eastern front and a corruption scandal.\n• A leaked US peace proposal in November, which would have seen Ukraine cede territory to Russia, alarmed Ukrainian and European officials.\n• European countries proposed a counter-proposal, and the US and Ukraine created an updated peace framework.\n• Putin accused European powers of trying to sink peace talks.\n• Ukraine and its allies accuse Putin of feigning interest in peace efforts.\n• NATO will continue supplying military aid to Ukraine.\n• The European Commission will move forward with plans to fund Ukraine with a loan based on Russia’s frozen assets.\n• The UN General Assembly voted for the return of Ukrainian children “forcibly transferred” to Russia; Russia rejected the measure.",
